  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A cart X of mass 3.0 kg moving at 6.0 m s<sup>−1</sup> collides with a stationary cart Y of mass 6.0 kg. A spring is attached to X as shown.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The graph shows the velocities of X and Y before, during and after the collision.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>The collision lasted for 40 ms.</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Show that the collision is elastic. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> Determine</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.i\"><p><strong>b.i</strong> the magnitude of the average force exerted on Y, [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.ii\"><p><strong>b.ii</strong> the average power delivered to Y, [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b.iii\"><p><strong>b.iii</strong> the elastic energy stored in the spring at t = 30 ms. [2]</p></section>"
  },
